// A card sent on (results.ent's COPY CARD and SHOW CARD), by the
// machine's own means (post.c): the picture put on the clipboard, to
// paste in a chat or a post, or the file shown in the file manager, to
// drag or attach. Each says whether it was done.
//
// - Windows: the clipboard as PNG and as a bitmap (some programs take
//   only the one), Explorer with the file selected;
// - macOS: the pasteboard as PNG and TIFF, Finder with the file
//   selected;
// - Linux: `wl-copy` (Wayland) or `xclip` (X) keep the picture for
//   pasting, also after the game has gone (a program that copies a
//   picture there must stay to give it); neither of them: not copied. The
//   file manager by its common call (FileManager1, with the file
//   selected), else the folder by `xdg-open`.
extern proc copy_picture(file: text[126]) -> bool
extern proc show_file(file: text[126]) -> bool
